WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.872
Welcome to Part 1 of the
implementation series

2
00:00:02.872 --> 00:00:05.912
for Ticket-to-Machine on
ServiceNow and SailPoint.

3
00:00:05.912 --> 00:00:10.312
The Federal Modernization Workbook's
Ticket-to-Machine loop is vendor-neutral.

4
00:00:10.312 --> 00:00:15.037
This guide builds it on two named products
to show what that takes, with ServiceNow

5
00:00:15.037 --> 00:00:19.762
as the front door and SailPoint Identity
Security Cloud for identity governance.

6
00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:22.175
It's an example, not an endorsement.

7
00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:24.675
The guide's argument fits in one line.

8
00:00:24.675 --> 00:00:28.725
Two products can carry the loop,
but neither one closes it alone.

9
00:00:28.725 --> 00:00:33.475
The ticket has to authorize a machine,
and only a re-read can close the ticket.

10
00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:38.394
Part 1 covers the first four gates: the
boundary, the writers and approvers,

11
00:00:38.394 --> 00:00:41.700
the sources and starting
drift, and the front door.

12
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.725
Part 2 covers actuation,
the re-read, and the tempo.

13
00:00:45.725 --> 00:00:48.675
The kit's tests run
against mocked responses.

14
00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:51.650
They prove the logic,
not the live integration.
